## Exact regressions

| Artifact / regression | What it rules out |
| --- | --- |
| Collective oblique chamber filling | A quadratic, triangle-free fixed-container filling can absorb one additional point, while its one-unit-protected region loses a linear capacity margin; this does not imply global optimality or source-preserving descent |
| Vanishing-shear oblique lattice | Density-only, local equilibrium, and fixed-angle-gap closures |
| Strict saturated chamber | One-point covering / near-pair matching / linear Oler slack alone |
| Co-embedded protected-erosion patch | Capacity plus contact-minimal covering alone, absent core coupling |
| Square-grid boundary/interface | Uniform local shortcut `a_r<=d_r+O(1)` or `a_r-d_r=o(d_r)` |
| One-anchor chamber retraction | First-contact rotation is not a valid triangle-free protected exchange |
| Finite arbitrary affine-window warning | No theorem may extend the D6 comparison to arbitrary index windows without a new hypothesis |
| Five-square two-direction plus stress | Positive local stress and hull-supported diameter reactions do not force a single rhombus; global optimality is the missing hypothesis |

## Rejected claims

- `G_loc=o(D²) => G_loc/d=o(1)`; the normalization is false.
- Contact creation or positive local KKT force automatically integrates to a finite release.
- A local jammed or rigid packing is a global minimum-diameter certificate.
- The full-source coordinate kernel equals the affine kernel on the nonisolated core.
- The inward contact pocket lies in the exterior Reuleaux cap.
- Diameter-edge incidence automatically supplies an Euler path.
- Numerical density or a carrier decimal alone settles the Level-I quantifiers.

## Current decisive obstruction

The canonical source-level alternatives remain:

```text
Type-I macroscopic inactive container/cap:
    saturated isolated population + covering
        -> missing core-coupled replacement or exact triangle

Type-II full core:
    aggregate detour floor + exceptional-face payment
    + full-core loaded-chord/train surplus floor mu>=1.6375621841815...
    + exact endpoint exclusion at mu_TC
        -> missing explicit gap / higher-surplus upper detour/deformation/triangle theorem
```

No entry in this ledger discharges either implication. The Level-I theorem is not
solved or disproved.
